WEBVTT

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:03.480
Huh?

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:05.770
R-Retraining?

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:07.650
Yup!

00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:11.950
You're off to the Karuizawa Training Institute!

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:13.530
Right.

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:17.120
You think they have good food there?

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:17.740
Huh?

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:19.620
Uh, who knows?

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:26.130
You'll be participating in the JNR PSF's advanced training.

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:26.920
Huh?

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:30.130
That's great for our resumes, right?

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:32.720
H-Hey!

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:35.840
There will be driving instruction as well.

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:36.970
Huh?

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:38.050
Really?!

00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:40.010
What's Karuizawa famous for?

00:00:40.430 --> 00:00:41.390
No way.

00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:42.730
The line through Usui Pass?

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:45.440
And the EF63 electric locomotive!

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:47.440
Let's go!

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:50.020
I just hope the food's all right.

00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:54.650
The pots-to-go they sell at
Yokokawa Station are very delicious.

00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:56.610
Let's eat!

00:00:57.070 --> 00:00:58.780
Are you going, Koumi?

00:00:58.780 --> 00:00:59.990
Oh, yes!

00:00:59.990 --> 00:01:02.370
If Takayama's going, IвЂ”

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:07.210
If everyone's going, I'll go.

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:10.090
Fourth Peacekeeper Squad trainees!

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:14.510
On the morn, we shall undergo the JNR PSF advanced training!

00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:16.970
Have fun!

00:02:55.190 --> 00:02:56.690
Awesome!

00:02:56.690 --> 00:02:58.150
It's the Usui Pass!

00:02:58.570 --> 00:02:58.950
The steepest slope of all JNR's rails!

00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:00.700
Station food's great!

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:04.120
Look, Sakurai!

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:07.200
Your drink's slanting!

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:08.580
That's how steep this thing is!

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:09.330
That was great!

00:03:09.330 --> 00:03:10.370
And we're <i>climbing</i> it!

00:03:10.370 --> 00:03:11.460
Oh yeah, we bought sweet bean mochi! Gimme that too!

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:13.840
Just feel yourself getting pulled down!

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:14.380
Thank you, gravity!

00:03:14.380 --> 00:03:15.040
Here.

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:15.670
Thank you!
Thank you, gravity!

00:03:15.670 --> 00:03:16.630
Oh, an arch bridge!

00:03:16.630 --> 00:03:19.050
Shut the hell up!

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:25.140
We're lucky it's so
close to the station.

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:26.600
I'm so hungry.

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:28.100
Seriously?

00:03:29.270 --> 00:03:31.480
We are the Fourth Peacekeeper Squad trainees!

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:33.980
Here to train, sir!

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:35.940
You made it in one piece I see, baby chicks.

00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:39.900
I'm Tetsuya Narita, and I'll be overseeing your training.

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:42.070
Gonou's told me all about you.

00:03:42.070 --> 00:03:45.070
You've got spunk to spare, it seems.

00:03:56.920 --> 00:03:58.170
Everything hurts.

00:03:58.170 --> 00:04:02.130
Training at JNR Central Academy
was a cakewalk compared to this.

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:04.470
Man, you're pathetic.

00:04:04.470 --> 00:04:05.220
Here, TakayamaвЂ”

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:07.180
Are you okay, Takayama?

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:09.890
Have some tea.

00:04:10.390 --> 00:04:14.690
You need food! Fill up your belly and
you'll be back on your feet in no time!

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:16.230
Can we order?

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:17.860
I'll be right there!

00:04:20.490 --> 00:04:21.990
Takayama!

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:23.990
Here for training?

00:04:23.990 --> 00:04:25.700
Yeah. You too, Sasshou?

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:28.910
Yup. But I never thought I'd run into you guys!

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:30.790
What a coincidence!

00:04:30.790 --> 00:04:31.870
No kidding.

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:35.880
Aren't you lucky, Takayama,
being surrounded by cute girls?

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:39.090
Are you calling yourself cute, Sakurai?

00:04:40.510 --> 00:04:41.960
What do you think you're doing?

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:43.970
So sorry. My hand slipped.

00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:46.260
That was totally on purpose!

00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:49.100
Hey, you serve curry here?

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:51.720
Yes. In fact, today's lunch special is katsu curry.

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:54.770
Nice! I'll have three extra big ones!

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:56.480
Guess I'll have the same.

00:04:56.480 --> 00:04:58.060
What about you, Takayama?

00:04:58.060 --> 00:04:59.820
I'll have what everyone else is having.

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:02.190
Then two more katsu curry, please.

00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:03.950
Coming right up.

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:06.450
Looks awesome!

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:08.200
Thank you for waiting.

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:10.200
Enjoy your meal.

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:11.990
Thank you!

00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:15.580
Huh?

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:17.920
How come only you get pickles, Takayama?

00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:18.630
Huh?

00:05:18.630 --> 00:05:20.920
Oh, I have this thing with leeks.

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:22.550
Oh yeah?

00:05:25.130 --> 00:05:27.390
She knows everything.

00:05:27.390 --> 00:05:29.890
God, you let people baby you too much!

00:05:30.260 --> 00:05:32.640
Hey, my pickles!

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:41.270
Right between the eyes, huh?

00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:45.530
I can shoot twice as many criminals with this instead of a revolver!

00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:47.240
You sure are motivated.

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:52.870
Weird.

00:05:54.040 --> 00:05:56.460
Nice shooting, if you're trying to warn them.

00:05:56.460 --> 00:05:58.000
Hey, Sakurai.

00:05:58.540 --> 00:06:00.540
Help him out, would you?

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:01.920
Fine.

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:04.050
Sorry, Sakurai.

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:06.920
Can't have you slowing me down.

00:06:06.920 --> 00:06:11.050
We're gonna be working together for a long time, after all.

00:06:11.050 --> 00:06:11.550
Huh?

00:06:11.550 --> 00:06:18.390
Taking the advanced training course means
you're basically guaranteed a future with the PSF.

00:06:19.060 --> 00:06:19.770
Wh-WhaвЂ”

00:06:21.110 --> 00:06:24.980
We might even end up assigned to the same division again.

00:06:24.980 --> 00:06:25.650
Here.

00:06:31.370 --> 00:06:34.120
So I'll suck it up for now.

00:06:41.130 --> 00:06:45.380
Since there's only one bath, we're supposed to decide who uses it first ourselves.

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:50.550
So how about the guys get it till 8 pm, and the girls after?

00:06:50.550 --> 00:06:52.010
Who cares? Food!

00:06:52.010 --> 00:06:53.600
I can't take it any longer!

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:54.930
See you later, gator.

00:06:54.930 --> 00:06:57.640
After all he ate today, he's still hungry?

00:06:58.100 --> 00:07:02.560
Iwaizumi moves around a lot,
so his metabolism must be really high.

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:06.480
And yet he never wastes a movement.

00:07:07.990 --> 00:07:11.110
You could learn a thing or two from him, Takayama.

00:07:11.110 --> 00:07:15.990
If you don't learn to save energy
while fighting, it'll come back to bite you.

00:07:15.990 --> 00:07:17.500
Huh? I'm notвЂ”

00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:21.000
I know! I'll help you with your personal training!

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:23.880
Need you to be able to keep up if we're gonna keep doing this.

00:07:24.290 --> 00:07:27.050
But I don't want to join the PSF.

00:07:27.050 --> 00:07:28.550
I want to be a train driver.

00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:29.590
Huh?

00:07:32.090 --> 00:07:34.300
Oh, uh, I meanвЂ”

00:07:35.050 --> 00:07:36.060
Shoot.

00:07:36.560 --> 00:07:39.680
You're not gonna join the PSF with us?

00:07:39.680 --> 00:07:42.230
But you're training with usвЂ”

00:07:42.230 --> 00:07:46.360
That's because I heard we'd get to drive an EF63.

00:07:46.360 --> 00:07:47.860
What the hell?

00:07:47.860 --> 00:07:48.690
Sorry.

00:07:49.030 --> 00:07:51.200
Then you should have said something!

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:52.610
You didn't complain when I was helping youвЂ”

00:07:52.610 --> 00:07:53.700
Well...

00:07:54.660 --> 00:07:57.830
You just seemed so happy.

00:07:59.040 --> 00:08:01.540
Wh-What's this got to do with me?

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:03.040
It's your own damn future!

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:05.210
Hey, wait a second!

00:08:05.210 --> 00:08:07.090
I said wait!

00:08:07.090 --> 00:08:08.380
Aoi.

00:08:12.590 --> 00:08:14.890
Man, what's up with Sakurai?

00:08:14.890 --> 00:08:17.970
What's wrong with wanting to be a train driver?

00:08:18.930 --> 00:08:20.520
I will be one.

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:21.730
Just like him.

00:08:24.270 --> 00:08:26.440
Oh, wow!

00:08:34.360 --> 00:08:35.740
My stomach...

00:08:38.780 --> 00:08:42.000
Hey, kid, that's dangerвЂ”

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:43.580
Hey!

00:08:43.580 --> 00:08:44.460
What's wrong, kid?

00:08:44.460 --> 00:08:45.750
You okay?

00:08:49.040 --> 00:08:51.090
Are you okay, Takayama?

00:08:51.090 --> 00:08:52.420
Takayama!

00:08:52.420 --> 00:08:53.340
Aoi!

00:08:53.340 --> 00:08:54.260
Come here!

00:08:54.590 --> 00:08:56.970
Aoi! Aoi!

00:08:58.260 --> 00:08:59.220
Aoi?

00:09:01.720 --> 00:09:04.310
What're you screaming for?

00:09:04.940 --> 00:09:07.310
Wh-What's he doing here?

00:09:07.310 --> 00:09:08.980
I think he passed out in the bath.

00:09:08.980 --> 00:09:12.900
What? Are you serious?

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:14.400
I'll get help.

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:15.990
Sakurai.

00:09:16.660 --> 00:09:18.370
I think he's hallucinating.

00:09:18.370 --> 00:09:20.740
He believes I'm you.

00:09:23.830 --> 00:09:26.790
Sakurai, listen to me.

00:09:29.170 --> 00:09:33.510
Long ago, someone inspired me to become a train driver.

00:09:33.960 --> 00:09:38.840
When I was a kid, I collapsed on a small, empty station way in the mountains due to stomach pains.

00:09:38.840 --> 00:09:40.180
He saved me.

00:09:41.010 --> 00:09:42.600
Hanging in there, kid?

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:44.730
We just have to get down this slope and you're home free.

00:09:44.730 --> 00:09:45.640
Keep fighting!

00:09:49.230 --> 00:09:55.150
If that driver hadn't noticed me back then,
who knows how my life would have turned out.

00:10:00.490 --> 00:10:03.740
I want to be like him...

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:11.750
A driver who appreciates life most of all...

00:10:14.340 --> 00:10:19.260
Don't worry. I'm sure Aoi understands.

00:10:21.350 --> 00:10:22.470
Aoi?

00:10:24.310 --> 00:10:25.850
I'm sorry about last night.

00:10:27.060 --> 00:10:28.810
You must think I'm a kid.

00:10:28.810 --> 00:10:29.940
I didn't check!

00:10:30.520 --> 00:10:32.940
I swear I didn't.

00:10:32.940 --> 00:10:36.190
Hey, did I say anything weird while I was out?

00:10:36.190 --> 00:10:36.940
No.

00:10:47.830 --> 00:10:53.290
The Usui Pass, which lies between Yokokawa and Karuizawa,
is the most dangerous segment of all JNR's rails.

00:10:53.290 --> 00:10:57.050
When it was first built, it used the Abt system of cogged track.

00:10:57.720 --> 00:11:01.720
In the center of the track lay
another rail with teeth,

00:11:01.720 --> 00:11:06.220
which the locomotive's gear would affix to and use to pull itself up.

00:11:06.220 --> 00:11:09.230
It only exists on the old line now, though.

00:11:10.520 --> 00:11:15.480
By the way, the line boasts
a maximum steepness of 66.7 permille.

00:11:15.480 --> 00:11:16.980
What's that?

00:11:16.980 --> 00:11:21.910
It means for every kilometer you go, you're also climbing 66 meters.

00:11:21.910 --> 00:11:23.070
That's a lot?

00:11:23.070 --> 00:11:24.450
Iwaizumi.

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:27.870
Give it some more respect.
That's one crazy slope for a train.

00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:33.250
And today, as special training,
you'll be driving this auxiliary locomotive.

00:11:33.250 --> 00:11:35.420
Y-You mean it?

00:11:35.420 --> 00:11:37.550
Let's get this over with and get some grub!

00:11:38.010 --> 00:11:39.760
Don't kill my buzz, man.

00:11:40.880 --> 00:11:43.840
Th-That's an ED42!

00:11:43.840 --> 00:11:46.220
I thought it'd be an EF63.

00:11:46.220 --> 00:11:48.100
Too old for you?

00:11:48.930 --> 00:11:50.060
Of course not!

00:11:50.060 --> 00:11:51.140
I'm honored!

00:11:52.350 --> 00:11:57.070
The Express Hakusan is led by
three ED42 electric locomotives

00:11:57.070 --> 00:12:01.450
followed by eight passenger cars, with the auxiliary car at its rear.

00:12:02.280 --> 00:12:04.030
Keep sharp when driving.

00:12:04.030 --> 00:12:04.910
Yes, sir!

00:12:04.910 --> 00:12:08.120
All right, decide who'll be in the rear car.

00:12:08.120 --> 00:12:08.950
Then...

00:12:08.950 --> 00:12:10.160
I'll do it.

00:12:10.160 --> 00:12:12.870
Wait! The rear car's the most difficult job!

00:12:13.290 --> 00:12:14.500
I said wait!

00:12:14.500 --> 00:12:17.460
We have to decide on our timings and whistle signs before starting!

00:12:17.460 --> 00:12:19.000
Don't bother.

00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:20.970
Just try and keep up.

00:12:22.130 --> 00:12:24.130
What's with her?

00:12:26.220 --> 00:12:28.680
The driver's seat is even better in person.

00:12:29.930 --> 00:12:32.690
This is my chance to show the brass my driving skills!

00:13:04.220 --> 00:13:06.890
Good. Now for the descent.

00:13:13.430 --> 00:13:15.190
What's with the random pulling?

00:13:15.770 --> 00:13:18.150
Sakurai gonna be okay back there?

00:13:18.150 --> 00:13:20.650
That means cut the power to the master controller.

00:13:32.160 --> 00:13:34.540
Hey, we're speeding up.

00:13:35.080 --> 00:13:37.250
I have to use dynamic braking too, huh?

00:13:45.130 --> 00:13:46.220
What was that?

00:13:49.430 --> 00:13:50.350
Hello?

00:13:50.350 --> 00:13:52.260
How do you use the brakes?

00:13:52.260 --> 00:13:53.720
Read the damn manual!

00:13:55.770 --> 00:13:56.440
What?!

00:13:56.440 --> 00:13:57.730
T-Takayama?

00:13:57.730 --> 00:13:59.310
Oh, Koumi?

00:13:59.310 --> 00:14:00.190
What is it?

00:14:00.190 --> 00:14:03.150
I think Aoi's pushing from behind.

00:14:03.150 --> 00:14:04.190
She is?

00:14:04.190 --> 00:14:06.820
All right. I'll signal her.

00:14:07.150 --> 00:14:09.780
Damn, what's she doing?

00:14:19.630 --> 00:14:21.460
Is she just screwing around?

00:14:21.460 --> 00:14:23.340
Hit the brake!

00:14:24.380 --> 00:14:27.300
What? You're the one dragging your ass!

00:14:33.470 --> 00:14:34.350
Why, you!

00:14:45.230 --> 00:14:48.490
This isn't good. We're just
going to keep accelerating.

00:14:48.490 --> 00:14:54.280
But if I brake any more, the connectors will be crushed and we'll derail!

00:14:56.750 --> 00:14:57.450
Hello?

00:14:57.450 --> 00:14:58.710
T-Takayama?

00:14:58.710 --> 00:15:00.710
We're really speeding up!

00:15:00.710 --> 00:15:03.040
I know. I'll try to fix it.

00:15:04.210 --> 00:15:05.750
Takayama, we going kinda fast?

00:15:05.750 --> 00:15:06.840
I know, damn it!

00:15:10.880 --> 00:15:13.100
At this rate we'll end up crashing.

00:15:13.640 --> 00:15:14.720
What do I do?

00:15:16.060 --> 00:15:18.140
I guess it's all or nothing.

00:15:25.320 --> 00:15:27.990
Stop!

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:42.750
Pretty realistic, don't you think?

00:15:42.750 --> 00:15:45.630
That's the JNR Virtual Simulator for you.

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:48.630
That was terrible.

00:15:49.210 --> 00:15:51.970
Go cool your heads and reflect.

00:15:51.970 --> 00:15:56.890
You forgot the most important thing for PSFвЂ”no, JNR employees.

00:15:56.890 --> 00:15:59.180
This accident is on all of your heads.

00:16:06.570 --> 00:16:11.570
I guess this just proves
I'm not cut out for the PSF.

00:16:12.200 --> 00:16:14.870
Much less deputy.

00:16:16.620 --> 00:16:17.740
Takayama.

00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:23.170
I'm almost done with work.

00:16:27.540 --> 00:16:28.710
Draw!

00:16:28.710 --> 00:16:29.960
Yes!

00:16:29.960 --> 00:16:31.420
Aw, the old maid again.

00:16:32.670 --> 00:16:34.800
Here, Takayama. Your turn.

00:16:36.010 --> 00:16:37.300
What'd you want to talk about?

00:16:39.060 --> 00:16:43.480
I think the PSF uniform suits you.
You look good in that.

00:16:43.480 --> 00:16:44.390
Huh?

00:16:48.440 --> 00:16:54.360
But right here, right now, you're kinda lame.

00:16:55.240 --> 00:16:58.830
Takayama, you should believe in yourself.

00:16:58.830 --> 00:17:01.620
And the rest of K4 are good people, too!

00:17:02.080 --> 00:17:03.290
Sasshou.

00:17:05.580 --> 00:17:07.790
Thanks for the advice.

00:17:07.790 --> 00:17:09.670
You're amazing.

00:17:09.670 --> 00:17:11.840
You really understand people's feelings.

00:17:17.550 --> 00:17:18.890
Takayama!

00:17:19.890 --> 00:17:21.060
Koumi?

00:17:21.060 --> 00:17:25.020
Mr. Narita just came by and said
we don't have training tomorrow.

00:17:25.560 --> 00:17:29.020
He said we won't accomplish anything if we keep this up.

00:17:29.020 --> 00:17:30.400
True.

00:17:30.400 --> 00:17:32.990
Then how about we all go out tomorrow?

00:17:32.990 --> 00:17:35.400
Take a break and explore the town!

00:17:35.400 --> 00:17:37.740
You're all the way out in Karuizawa, after all.

00:17:37.740 --> 00:17:39.240
Good idea!

00:17:39.240 --> 00:17:42.700
We should invite Iwaizumi and Aoi, too.

00:17:42.700 --> 00:17:45.580
Then inviting Sakurai should be...

00:17:45.580 --> 00:17:48.500
...the deputy's job, right?

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:49.210
Huh?

00:17:53.630 --> 00:17:54.720
I can't!

00:17:54.720 --> 00:17:56.340
I'm so pathetic.

00:17:59.640 --> 00:18:00.550
What's this?

00:18:04.140 --> 00:18:05.140
Her, huh?

00:18:13.070 --> 00:18:18.280
What do you think? I didn't bring anything since we were just training.

00:18:19.280 --> 00:18:21.200
I had to buy this in a hurry.

00:18:21.200 --> 00:18:22.780
Is it all right?

00:18:22.780 --> 00:18:25.950
It's better than just all right.

00:18:25.950 --> 00:18:27.460
Right, Iwaizumi?

00:18:27.460 --> 00:18:29.670
I can't find any restaurants!

00:18:29.670 --> 00:18:32.380
That's really all you think about, huh?

00:18:32.380 --> 00:18:35.340
If you don't mind Italian,
there's a good place close by.

00:18:35.340 --> 00:18:36.590
All right! We go there!

00:18:37.970 --> 00:18:40.590
No comment for me?

00:18:40.590 --> 00:18:43.430
I already know you look
cute in anything, Sasshou.

00:18:43.430 --> 00:18:44.510
What was that?

00:18:45.140 --> 00:18:47.980
Don't think that counts as a compliment!

00:18:49.640 --> 00:18:51.650
So, is Sakurai coming?

00:18:51.650 --> 00:18:53.610
Well, I invited her.

00:18:53.940 --> 00:18:56.440
I hope you two make up soon.

00:19:00.160 --> 00:19:01.530
The K4 office?

00:19:02.280 --> 00:19:03.080
Hello?

00:19:03.080 --> 00:19:05.370
Are you enjoying your vacation?

00:19:05.370 --> 00:19:06.330
Ms. Iida?

00:19:06.790 --> 00:19:11.080
I'm sorry to interrupt,
but can I ask you a favor?

00:19:11.500 --> 00:19:16.590
There's someone important
I want you to pick up.

00:19:16.960 --> 00:19:21.090
They insisted it had to be you!

00:19:21.970 --> 00:19:25.310
Okay. The church, right?

00:19:26.100 --> 00:19:28.350
Roger that.

00:19:28.350 --> 00:19:29.600
Was there an incident?

00:19:30.020 --> 00:19:32.810
Nah. Just a favor.

00:19:32.810 --> 00:19:34.770
I'll come with you.

00:19:34.770 --> 00:19:37.860
It's okay. It's really no big deal.

00:19:38.360 --> 00:19:40.990
I'll meet up with you guys
when I'm done. Go on.

00:19:40.990 --> 00:19:41.950
But...

00:19:41.950 --> 00:19:44.240
Sakurai will probably show up soon, too.

00:19:44.240 --> 00:19:46.790
If she calls, I'll direct her to you guys.

00:19:46.790 --> 00:19:47.620
Bye!

00:19:48.160 --> 00:19:49.080
Takayama!

00:19:49.080 --> 00:19:51.460
I'll be right back! See ya!

00:19:51.460 --> 00:19:52.620
See ya!

00:20:03.050 --> 00:20:04.220
Sakurai?

00:20:04.890 --> 00:20:06.220
She came?

00:20:07.470 --> 00:20:11.140
Wait, I didn't ask where the restaurant was.

00:20:11.140 --> 00:20:12.270
Oh well.

00:20:23.160 --> 00:20:24.320
This the place?

00:20:29.160 --> 00:20:29.830
Huh?

00:20:30.500 --> 00:20:31.790
No one's here.

00:20:35.460 --> 00:20:37.040
What's going on?

00:20:39.250 --> 00:20:40.510
Takayama.

00:20:44.630 --> 00:20:45.800
I'm here.

00:20:48.640 --> 00:20:50.770
S-Sakurai?

00:20:51.980 --> 00:20:54.440
Haruka and the others aren't with you?

00:20:54.440 --> 00:20:55.270
Huh?

00:20:55.270 --> 00:20:56.440
Oh, uh...

00:21:03.700 --> 00:21:06.070
I'm surprised you're dressed up like that.

00:21:06.070 --> 00:21:08.530
What's it to you? I like this stuff too.

00:21:09.700 --> 00:21:13.000
But why'd you want to meet me at a church?

00:21:13.330 --> 00:21:15.710
What're you thinking?

00:21:15.710 --> 00:21:17.420
No, uh...

00:21:18.920 --> 00:21:20.250
Koumi?

00:21:20.250 --> 00:21:21.460
What're you doing here?

00:21:22.090 --> 00:21:23.510
What's the meaning of this?

00:21:24.260 --> 00:21:28.350
I thought I'd help you with your work.

00:21:28.890 --> 00:21:32.270
But then I find you meeting
Aoi in an empty church!

00:21:32.270 --> 00:21:34.430
K-Koumi?

00:21:34.430 --> 00:21:36.730
You even lied!

00:21:37.100 --> 00:21:39.110
I never thought you'd lie to me!

00:21:39.110 --> 00:21:40.230
No...

00:21:40.230 --> 00:21:41.070
No, that's not it!

00:21:41.070 --> 00:21:43.530
You lied? What's she talking about?

00:21:43.530 --> 00:21:44.360
Yes.

00:21:45.200 --> 00:21:46.780
An explanation is in order.

00:21:49.870 --> 00:21:51.620
N-Noa?

00:21:52.910 --> 00:21:57.790
I said I wanted <i>you</i> waiting for me.

00:21:59.250 --> 00:22:02.880
So what are Sakurai and Koumi doing here?

00:23:40.770 --> 00:23:44.230
On extreme slopes, an auxiliary engine is connected

00:23:44.230 --> 00:23:47.480
to assist in hauling and braking
the train going uphill and downhill.

00:23:48.030 --> 00:23:51.070
The JNR ED42 series electric locomotive that runs

00:23:51.070 --> 00:23:54.660
through the Usui Pass between Yokokawa and Karuizawa is a prominent example.

00:23:54.660 --> 00:23:58.540
Coordinated, manual operation between the auxiliary and main engines is required,

00:23:58.540 --> 00:24:00.080
and the driver's skill is tested to its limitsвЂ”

00:24:00.080 --> 00:24:01.210
We're out of time!

00:24:01.210 --> 00:24:02.330
Hurry!

00:24:02.330 --> 00:24:05.500
Rail Wars, Episode Eight: I'll Do It!

00:24:05.840 --> 00:24:08.550
You focus on driving, Takayama!
